  ],
  "scope": "Exact prospective source-integration statement: actual unique stationary proximal witness, actual canonical finite relative entropy, canonical llr L1 and AE explicit logdensity, actual rho L1 and two real entropy formulas. Narrow internally authored analytic/coherence background for the printed first4.6 invocation, not a separately printed full theorem.",
  "seven_semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "One existential measurable p; literal rho from this p; mu=volume.tilted(-V); actual R=mu.tilted(-norm(x-y)^2/(2eta)); r=R.map((x-p)/sqrt eta); gamma=stdGaussian E; Z=integral_gamma exp(-rho); q=exp(-rho)/Z. Canonical InformationTheory.klDiv(r,gamma) and MeasureTheory.llr(r,gamma), not a selected smooth replacement divergence.",
    "domains": "Finite complete real Hilbert/Borel E, including zero dimension; same normalized actual C2 Hessian V and kappa>=1; every eta(s)>0. Current32 internally supplies actual positive Z, actual probability r, r=gamma.tilted(-rho), positive explicit q and q log q L1 gamma. No public probability/normalizer/integrability/LSI/T2 certificates.",
    "quantifiers": "For arbitrary stated E and declared authored measurable S family, eta and y satisfy their measurability and pointwise eta>0; exists one p with all displayed laws defined from that p; pointwise every s; uniqueness every z:E satisfying the same stationarity equation. No joint kernel law or stochastic-family independence asserted.",
    "assumptions": "Printed standing C2 V and normalized curvature kappa^-1 I<=Hess V<=I; positive eta. Hilbert/Borel classes are carrier typing. S and measurable eta/y are disclosed inherited authored family extension, whose Unit constant specialization has no extra source premise. No undocumented binder, Prop alias, probability, integrability, concentration, selector or mean certificate.",
    "conclusion": "Same p stationary and uniquely stationary; actual r<<gamma; canonical ENNReal KL !=top; canonical llr L1 under actual r; canonical llr=log q only r-a.e.; rho L1 under r; canonical KL.toReal=integral_gamma q log q=-integral_r rho-log Z. This is a measure/domain/coherence endpoint, not Gaussian LSI/T2 or W2.",
    "scope_and_sense": "Uniqueness is an internally derived conclusion that permits future identification of stationary existential witnesses; the statement does not assume unrelated old witnesses are definitionally identical. AE llr equality transfers integrability/integrals only. It does not imply pointwise derivatives of the canonical RN representative.",
    "constant_dependencies": "gamma covariance I, standardized scale sqrt eta, rho linear term sqrt eta times inner(grad V(p),u), R quadratic denominator 2eta. Relative partition Z is Gaussian-relative and used exactly once. KL=-E_r rho-log Z has no original V partition or affine Jacobian term. Every positive eta allowed; numerical proximal algorithm cap is separate."
  },
